.TH GIT-REVIEW 1
.SH NAME
git-review \- open a code review for the current branch, auto-detecting the platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git review
.RI [ target-branch ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git review
opens a code review for the current branch, auto-detecting the platform from the
.B origin
remote URL.
When
.I target-branch
is omitted, the remote default branch from
.B origin/HEAD
is used (falling back to
.BR main ).
.PP
Platform detection happens in priority order:
.TP
.B GitHub
URL contains
.BR github.com :
push the branch and run
.B gh pr create --fill --base <target>
.RB ( gh
CLI required).
.TP
.B Alibaba GitLab
URL contains
.BR alibaba :
push Gerrit-style to
.BR refs/for/<target>/<current-branch> .
Matched before generic GitLab.
.TP
.B GitLab
URL contains
.BR gitlab :
push with server-side merge-request options
.RB ( merge_request.create ,
.BR merge_request.target ).
.TP
.B Gerrit
otherwise: push to
.BR refs/for/<target> .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git review
    Open a review against the remote default branch.

git review main
    Open a review targeting main.

git review release/1.0
    Open a review targeting release/1.0.
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-rb (1),
.BR git-bc (1),
.BR git-wc (1)
